{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>For</b> — the vav of חיתו is superfluous, like the vav in עור." "<b>Upon the mountains of a thousand</b> — a thousand mountains, or a thousand parasangs, or the name [means] a thousand bulls. And Rabbi Moses said: it is like שגר אלפיך, mountains full of cattle, because he mentioned [the word] bull."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 50, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:31:26.438560431Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}